A||||17||theogre||DEFECT! Chime Box.||||1||
Z||000000||theogre||09-04-2000||03:41 PM||||There is a manufacturing defect in the chime unit that likely affects millions of units. I've sent Cliff an update to the chime page in my cave with all the details. He should have it up in the next day or so.<P>In brief. There is a problem with the design of the circuit board that results in a weak connection. When the connection cracks it can manifest in any or all the following ways...<P>Dead chime, may just be so weak you can't hear it unlees you are very close.<P>weak or staticy chime tones, may be intermitant.<P>random tones. (Still checking this one to make sure.)<P>New or Used replacement boxes are likely to have the same cracked connection. The connection can be fixed fairly easy.<P>To prevent the crack opening again make sure you handle chime units only by the narrow sides. Squeezing the largest sides flexes the board and can open the joint.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bill Osmer||09-04-2000||08:13 PM||||Ogre -<P>I checked the "Cave" but didn't see any specifics as to FIXING the problem. Since you allude to a circuit that is probably cracked/intermittebtly open, could you post more info on the specific location? A picture of the location would be great, so that people handy with a soldering iron can fix the darn thing!!!<P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000002||Songman||09-04-2000||08:45 PM||||Ogre,<BR>Again, I hear mention of your 'cave'. Where is this? Sounds like lots of info there that I would love to see.<P>Also, I have problem in my 88 coupe of an intermittent chime that sounds like a headlight on chime or something. It happens going down the road. There seems to be no pattern to it. Is this what you are talking about here? I figured it was something to do with my tilt column being loose. That is another problem I need to fix. Any suggestions?<P>Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000003||My7Fieros||09-04-2000||10:24 PM||||Cool, thanx Ogre.<BR>Songman, to locate Ogres cave, scroll down to the bottom of the page and youll see a link. I had the same prob. with the chime box in my 88...week sounding chime, chimes for no reason, I just pulled the thing.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||09-04-2000||10:25 PM||||The link to ogres house is at the bottom of the page.  Click on "Ogre's Cave".  It's between "Contact Us/Back to Main Menu" and the PIP link.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||09-04-2000||11:23 PM||||The page that's there now (23:00 04-Sep-00)is the old one. The defect isn't in it.<P>The update for the page was sent up this afternoon. Cliff will get to it as soon as he has time. Give him a couple days.<P>Bill,<BR>Wait for Cliff to get the article posted for me. There's more detail in it. <P>The location of the crack is very clear. It's on the chime board. Very easy to find. look at the end of the support for the chime speaker near the terminal end of the board. It can be cracked without really showing much so rework the joint anyway. (You have to be careful. It's a heavy connection and you can cook the trace off the board easily.) make sure you don't bridge solder to adjacent terminals. there's not allot of space between them.<P>I'll try to post a picture. It will be faster if someone with a digital camera can send me a clear close in picture of the solder side of the chime unit circuit board. Then I can just point out the defect spot. Otherwise you'll have to wait untill I use up the film in our camera.<P>Song,<BR>Yes this may be part of the random tone problem described in the chime article. And that you describe above.(As his Monkeyness said, The link to the cave is at the bottom of every forum page.) I just fixed a chime box today and haven't driven the car enough to verify that the random tones are also gone.<P>Notes about the loose tilt unit are also in my cave. I generally don't recomend most people fool with it. Used columns are not very expencive or hard to install.<P>My7, <BR>Pulling the box is a solution. Doing that presents problems of its own. For one thing if you lock the headlights up in bad weather it's really easy to forget when they are actually on since you can't go by the position of the headlight door. Plus we have some forum members who have family members that are partly blind and can't see the brake warning lamp glowing at them.<P>Right now I have all signal lines but the seat belt chime wire connected. (Now that one is just bloody annoying. Rather pointless since it only watches the drivers seatbelt.) I'll drive the car over the next few days and see how it goes. If the random tones are gone I'll hook the seatbelt back up just to make sure it's not that line.<P><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||09-05-2000||02:12 PM||||Well, so far today I drove over some fairly scaggy road and not one false ding. I'll drive it the rest of the week and see if anything shows up. So far it looks like the cracked connection may be the main source of the random tone problem. ((There are a couple other things that can cause it. Like a pinched hand brake wire.))<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||09-06-2000||05:26 PM||||Thanks to Bill Osmer I have a picture that is now marked with the defective area.<P>It hase a temporary home here --&gt; <A HREF="http://home.sprynet.com/~theogre/image/chime.jpg" TARGET=_blank>Defect Picture</A><BR>I've left the picture rather large so people could see the detail better. It's 138K so give it a minute or 3 if you are using a modem.<P>I have some other pictures to post on a roll of film so this picture won't be in the fiero branch of my cave untill next week.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cliff Pennock||09-06-2000||06:05 PM||||Page has been updated. Sorry it took so long.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||overlord||09-06-2000||08:09 PM||||in my fiero i only hear the box chime when the lights are left on.....i thought tahts all the diging and beeping there was supposed to be.......until one day was driving and all of a sudden "ding ding ding", look at the flashing light..and twas the seatbelt light.      never heard it before.||||reg||1
Z||000010||fierocrazy||09-06-2000||09:56 PM||||my 85GT chimes only when I first take off, is this the defect you are talking about?<P>85GT 3.2||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||09-07-2000||12:28 AM||||Thanks Cliff. That version has most of the details. I'll have one final update of it next week before I return to work. (YEAH!!!!! I'm so bored.)<P><BR>The defect is agravated by vibration. What both Overlord and Fierocrazy are describing are posible.<P>The defect joint causes power distribution problems on the board. Depending just how bad the crack is and how it forms determines allot of how flaky the box will be. There's no single way for the joint to crack. Some of the cracks are clearly visible. Others had no visible crack but when the joint was reworked the chime worked perfect.<P>It's also entirely posible some boxes have more than one crack. If one of the input terminals is cracked it can have similar effects. So far I've not seen a terminal cracked. They are much better attached.<P>Of the 2 boxes I presently have. (I wish I saved them all.) One was visibly cracked and was completely nuts. The other was not visibly cracked but still gave a random ding at least once a week. (I'll grab more boxes from the salvage yard as soon as I can.)<P>I repaired the worst one and so far have not seen one trace of problems. This box used to give me crap as soon as I started driving off.||||reg||1
Z||000012||fierocrazy||09-07-2000||10:36 PM||||i am confussed, where do I get the info for the chime board, my chime will chime randomly once and awhile, thanks<P>85GT 3.2||||reg||1
Z||000013||theogre||09-07-2000||11:40 PM||||Read the article in the cave. It's got most of the details about the problem. Cliff just got it posted yesterday. That or wait untill next week when I send the final version.<P>You need the picture I linked in a message above. You need to fix the solder joint indicated in that picture. (The picture was not ready for the cave at the time I sent the article to Cliff. It will be in the final version.) You need decent soldering skills or someone else that has them. If this repair is botched you'll likely short the box out or damage it with the soldering iron.||||reg||1
Z||000014||theogre||09-19-2000||10:44 PM||||I thought I'd pull this back out.....<P>Good news. Since fixing the cracked joint in the chime box a couple weeks ago I've not had one single random tone. Even when driving on really rough pavement.<P>I think we've finally got the thing beat.||||reg||6
Z||000015||theogre||09-21-2000||02:19 PM||||<B>NOTICE!!!</B><P>It has come to my attention that there are 2(TWO) versions of chime box!<P>The Old style one has a door that opens to expose the whole back of the chime board. (I now have one of this box for testing.) It is unknown at this time what if any defects apply to the old style box.<P>The New style has a door that opens on the small end oposite the terminals. (It is pictured in the Fiero Tech Zone pictures.) It is this new style box that is affeected by the defect.||||reg||1
Z||000016||theogre||10-05-2000||09:00 AM||||Here's an update some might find interesting.<P>on the old style chime box are listed a couple of the US patent numbers thay apply to it. So I went to <A HREF="http://www.uspto.gov" TARGET=_blank>www.uspto.gov</A>  and ran a search. I found the full name of the company.<P>Then I went to HotBot and ran a search on Lectron Products (set it for "exact phrase" not the default "all the words.")<P>These guys aparantly make allot of crap for the car makers. I got back all sorts of things about them. A press release from JD edwards that has a paragraph about them. More patents. even saw resumes of former employees. So far everything but a web site for them. That may be there but farther down than I've looked in the list.<P><BR>side note: I took a picture of the 2 chime versions. I'll add that to the defect page in the cave on the next update.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||Carrolles||10-05-2000||09:14 AM||||Theogre,<P>Thanks for all your work on this issue.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
